{"slug":"pyrola-rotundifolia","plant":{"taxon":"Pyrola rotundifolia","family":"Ericaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":2888269,"wikidata":"Q692248","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":113719,"common_name":"Round-leaved wintergreen","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Winter-Green","monograph_id":"cul:144-winter-green","confidence":"medium","note":"Pear-like leaves, open star-like fragrant white flowers, northern woods; Pyrola."}],"n_compounds":20,"top_compounds":[{"name":"apocynin","qid":"Q414754"},{"name":"ursolic acid","qid":"Q416260"},{"name":"methylhydroquinone","qid":"Q1925586"},{"name":"hyperoside","qid":"Q5242815"},{"name":"4-hydroxy acetophenone","qid":"Q7190613"},{"name":"chimaphilin","qid":"Q27106145"},{"name":"Pyrolaside B","qid":"Q27135430"},{"name":"Homoarbutin","qid":"Q72482576"}],"epmc_total":20,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":3,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.97,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"wounds","dsc":0,"cul":3,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.75,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhage","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.66,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"inflammation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":1.48,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"kidney_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":2.16,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"menorrhagia","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:144-winter-green":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Winter-Green","headword":"Winter-Green","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"Winter-green is under the dominion of Saturn, and is a singularly good wound herb, and an especial remedy for healing green wounds speedily, the green leaves being bruised and applied, or the juice of them. A salve made of the green herb stamped, or the juice boiled with hog’s lard, or with salad oil and wax, and some turpentine added to it, is a sovereign salve, and highly extolled by the Germans, who use it to heal all manner of wounds and sores. The herb boiled in wine and water, and given to drink to them that have any inward ulcers in their kidneys, or neck of the bladder, doth wonderfully help them. It stays all fluxes, as the lask, bloody fluxes, women’s courses, and bleeding of wounds, and takes away any inflammations rising upon pains of the heart; it is no less helpful for foul ulcers hard to be cured; as also for cankers or fistulas. The distilled water of the herb effectually performs the same things.","spans":[{"start":71,"end":76,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":124,"end":130,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":435,"end":441,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":446,"end":451,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":552,"end":559,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":576,"end":583,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":616,"end":677,"concept_id":"menorrhagia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":683,"end":691,"concept_id":"hemorrhage","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":695,"end":701,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":722,"end":735,"concept_id":"inflammation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":799,"end":805,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":836,"end":843,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":847,"end":855,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"images":[]}